    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Hồ Chí Minh proclaimed the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> on 2 September 1945; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a>, aided by Chinese communists from 1949, defeated the French at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Battle of Dien Bien Phu</a> in 1954, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Accords left it the zone north of the 17th parallel.</li><li>Its land reform of 1953–1956 gave land to poor and landless peasants but was carried out with violence; estimates of the executions range from a few thousand to far higher, and Hồ Chí Minh apologised for its errors on 18 August 1956.</li><li>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-duan">Lê Duẩn</a> from 1960 it waged war on the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-cong">Viet Cong</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> trail, and after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> in 1975 the two halves were reunited as the Socialist Republic of Vietnam in 1976.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/politburo">Politburo</a> document dated 4 May 1953 fixed the planned executions of the land reform &quot;in principle at the ratio of one per one thousand people of the total population&quot;.</p></aside>
    </section>

