ber, and in December the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war">First Indochina War</a> begins as the French reoccupy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1953</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> Land Reform Law of 4 December opens the land reform, carried out until 1956</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1954</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-minh">Viet Minh</a> defeat the French at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Battle of Dien Bien Phu</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva">Geneva</a> Accords divide <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> provisionally along the 17th parallel</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1956</span><span class="rf-text">Hồ Chí Minh apologises on 18 August for the errors of the land reform, and rioting against its excesses breaks out in a largely Catholic district in November</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1960</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-duan">Lê Duẩn</a>'s leadership begins, and the North goes to war with the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> through its proxy the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viet-cong">Viet Cong</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1975</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> falls on 30 April, and South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> comes under the Provisional Revolutionary Government</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1976</span><span class="rf-text">North and South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> are officially reunited on 2 July as the Socialist Republic of Vietnam</span></li></ol>
